remstart
    CAMEOS
    some of the words that can be tapped out on the radio do nothing but bring somebody through:
    a fish, or a few of them, or something bigger, that swims across the screen from the left to the
    right, and is gone. nothing in the game says that these words are there, but the radio gives one
    of them away, a new one every time, when it answers CQ: see morseReplyStart. see MORSE in
    fish_headers. the routines are in fish_routines_cameo, and the tests are in fish_tests_cameo.

    THE WORDS. these are all of them:
        NEMO        -.  .  --  ---                          a clown fish, and a blue fish that comes after it
        FREDDI      ..-.  .-.  .  -..  -..  ..              a yellow fish, and a little green one that keeps up with it
        U571        ..-  .....  --...  .----                a submarine, with a ping
        WILLY       .--  ..  .-..  .-..  -.--               the shadow of a whale goes over, with its call
        PEARL       .--.  .  .-  .-.  .-..                  a black ship goes by, up at the top
        DOPEFISH    -..  ---  .--.  .  ..-.  ..  ...  ....  a green fish with two big teeth
        JAWS        .---  .-  .--  ...                      a fin, along the bottom, faster and faster, with two low notes
        ARIEL       .-  .-.  ..  .  .-..                    a fork, turning over and over, and a mermaid who is after it
        MYLEG       --  -.--  .-..  .  --.                  nobody comes, but somebody, somewhere, shouts "my leg!"

    A SWIMMER is one thing that crosses. a word has one of them, or two, but for MYLEG, which
    has none: it is only heard, a moment after the radio has said that it was received. setup_cameo makes every
    swimmer of every word, each with its own sprite, and they wait, hidden. when a word is heard, its
    swimmers set off (cameoStart), and cameoStep moves them, on every frame of the game. a swimmer
    takes its own time to cross, and may wait a moment before it sets off, so that it comes after
    the other one. it bobs up and down as it goes. the fin of JAWS starts slow and gets faster, and
    the fork of ARIEL turns over as it goes.
    a word that is sent again while its swimmers are out starts them over, from the left.
    the swimmers go over the fish of the board, and under the words and numbers around it: see
    ORDER_HUD_TEXT in fish_headers.

    IN THE CODEC. every word has an entry, after the night, in the order of the words. it is locked
    until the word is sent, the same as the entry that SING and SONG share is. its picture is whoever the
    word brings. see CODEC_ENTRY_CAMEO in fish_headers, and cameoWord.

    a new word is a line here, a number like MORSE_WORD_NEMO in fish_headers and a morseWord in
    setup_morse, a cameoWord and a cameoSwimmer or two in setup_cameo, and one more in
    CODEC_EXTRA_COUNT. the words must stay in a row, from MORSE_WORD_NEMO to MORSE_WORD_MYLEG, and
    a new one goes on the end, so that the ones before it keep their preferences.

    the pictures that the game did not have are drawn by Tools/cameo_art_gen.py, and the two sounds
    are made by Tools/cameo_sounds_gen.py. none of it is taken from the films, the shows or the
    games that the words are from.
remend
` on top of the fish, and underneath the words around the board and the bubbles. it is only one more than ORDER_FISH,
` and that is enough: the swimmers are made thousands of sprites after the fish are, which the engine counts
` as a few more in the order. see ORDER_HUD_TEXT in fish_headers. the tests check that it still comes out right.
global ORDER_CAMEO = 21
global CAMEO_ROOM = 16 `how many swimmers there can be, over all of the words
global CAMEO_COUNT = 0 `how many there are
global CAMEO_LIVE = 0 `how many of them are out, or waiting to set off
global dim CAMEO_WORD(16) `the word that every swimmer comes for
global dim CAMEO_SPRITE(16)
global dim CAMEO_WIDE(16) `how wide it is drawn, in pixels of the game
global dim CAMEO_Y(16) `how far down the screen it crosses
global dim CAMEO_LIFE_MS(16) `how long it takes to cross
global dim CAMEO_WAIT_MS(16) `how long after the word it sets off
global dim CAMEO_BOB(16) `how far it bobs, up and down, in pixels
global dim CAMEO_RUSH(16) `1 for one that starts slow and gets faster
global dim CAMEO_SPIN(16) `1 for one that turns over and over
global dim CAMEO_ON(16) `1 while it is out, or waiting to set off
global dim CAMEO_START_MS(16) `when it sets off
global dim CAMEO_X(16) `where it is right now
global dim CAMEO_HEARD(24) `how many times each word has brought its swimmers out
global CAMEO_BOB_RATE# = .003 `how fast they bob
global CAMEO_SPIN_RATE# = .0016 `and how fast the ones that turn over do, in radians for every millisecond
global CAMEO_WORD_COUNT = 0 `how many of the words there are. the first is MORSE_WORD_NEMO, and they are in a row.
global dim CAMEO_ICON_TEX(16) `for every one of the words, counting from 0: the picture that it has in the codec,
global dim CAMEO_ICON_W(16) `how big that picture is, in its own pixels,
global dim CAMEO_ICON_H(16)
global dim CAMEO_NAME$(16) `what the codec calls it, as a key of cameo.csv,
global dim CAMEO_SAYS$(16) `and what the codec says about it, after how it is tapped out, as a key too
global TEX_CAMEO_CLOWN `the pictures. the first two, and the whale, are fish that the game has anyway.
global TEX_CAMEO_TANG
global TEX_CAMEO_FREDDI
global TEX_CAMEO_SUB
global TEX_CAMEO_SHIP
global TEX_CAMEO_DOPEFISH
global TEX_CAMEO_FIN
global TEX_CAMEO_FORK
global TEX_CAMEO_MERMAID
global SFX_CLIP_CAMEO_JAWS `the two low notes of JAWS
global SFX_CAMEO_JAWS = 0
global CAMEO_JAWS_VOLUME# = .55 `how loud they are. the same as JAWS_VOLUME in Tools/cameo_sounds_gen.py.
global CAMEO_JAWS_MS = 9000 `how long they go on for, and so how long the fin takes. the same as JAWS_LENGTH there.
global SFX_CLIP_CAMEO_LEG `and the shout of MYLEG
global SFX_CAMEO_LEG = 0
global CAMEO_LEG_VOLUME# = .7 `the same as LEG_VOLUME there
global CAMEO_LEG_AT_MS = 1900 `how long after the word the shout comes: when the radio has tapped its R
global CAMEO_LEG_DUE = 0 `1 while the shout is on its way
global CAMEO_LEG_MS = 0 `when it comes
global CAMEO_LEG_COUNT = 0 `how many times it has been shouted
